Provenance of the N64 renderer (runtime/guests/n64/rdp)

prdp.cpp drives parallel-rdp, https://github.com/Themaister/parallel-rdp,
which relift does not vendor: `relift build` fetches the standalone tree
https://github.com/Themaister/parallel-rdp-standalone at commit
388d70f5835b352d841d9d9e5a08c5de01470f41 (parallel-rdp
1cecd042b2619bc505c12bfdc713808386f2b54d) by URL, checks its SHA-256
(relift/src/parallel_rdp.rs) and builds it into every N64 program. Its
shaders come precompiled as SPIR-V in that tree; nothing is compiled at run
time. The tree carries parallel-rdp and its Vulkan backend (MIT, text 1),
volk (MIT, text 2) and the Vulkan headers (Apache-2.0, headers only). Every
N64 program built by relift carries these notices in licenses/ beside it.

How prdp.cpp sets up the processor follows ares, n64/vulkan/vulkan.cpp, at
the commit and under the ISC license named in ../NOTICE.

